WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.288
Teacher midterm practice, question 12.

2
00:00:03.908 --> 00:00:07.097
In Figure 1, at which point does the metal begin to neck?

3
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:12.878
Necking starts at the maximum engineering stress, the tensile strength.

4
00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.023
That is point D.

5
00:00:14.643 --> 00:00:17.379
Before D, strain hardening outpaces the loss

6
00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:20.401
of area, so the deformation stays uniform.

7
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:23.137
After D, it concentrates in the neck.

8
00:00:24.736 --> 00:00:26.572
The answer is C: point D.

9
00:00:27.392 --> 00:00:29.612
Necking does not start at yield.

10
00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:33.768
Between B and D the deformation is plastic, but still uniform.
